Independently reproduced on today's `origin/main` — and there is one thing in the proposed fix that will silently keep the bug if it isn't done too.

Environment: upstream `a15e5765` (2026-10-16), Windows/amd64, go1.27.0, `go test -tags nogui`.

## Reproduction

A test that only uses existing symbols, so it is a real red on the unmodified base, not a compile error:

```
=== RUN   TestCodexModelListKeepsFreshWindowOnTimeout
    codex_native_timeout_window_test.go:69: gpt-6.1-sol context_window 272000 after the timeout, want the cached 500000
--- FAIL: TestCodexModelListKeepsFreshWindowOnTimeout (0.49s)
```

It seeds `catalog.SaveLive("codex", …)` with 272000, puts a 500000 `gpt-6.1-sol` in `$CODEX_HOME/models_cache.json`, points `provider.CodexBase` at an `httptest` server that never answers, sets `codexModelsWait = 200ms`, and asks `GET /v1/models?client_version=0.162.0`.

## Where it happens

`internal/gateway/codex_backend.go`, `codexModels`:

- `codexModelsWait = 3s` (`:1225`), used for the upstream request (`:1237`).
- A success stores the raw list (`:1248-1252`); a timeout leaves `own == nil`.
- `cached := own == nil` (`:1267`) → the fallback list comes from `codexcat.CacheEntries()` (`:1269`), i.e. Codex's own rendered cache, which still says 500000.
- `window := provider.CodexNativeWindow(cached)` (`:1276`) is then applied to *every* entry.

`internal/provider/codex_models.go:567-587`, `CodexNativeWindow(restore bool)`: when the provider has no explicit window for a slug and `restore` is true, it answers from `catalog.Live("codex")` — the provider's own list, last fetched a day ago, still 272000. That is what overwrites the cached 500000.

## The catch in the proposed fix

Saving a snapshot of the successful raw list and serving it on failure is the right shape, but if that path is then run through `CodexNativeWindow(true)` as well, the live fallback in `:577-584` puts 272000 straight back on top of the snapshot — the snapshot would be correct and the answer still wrong. The restore step has to be off for the snapshot path (`CodexNativeWindow(false)`), or the snapshot has to be something the live fallback can't overwrite.

Two smaller things: `own` is mutated in place by the window step and the pick filter, so the snapshot needs a deep copy; and the snapshot key really does need the user/workspace dimension, because `catalog.Live("codex")` is per account and two accounts can have different official windows.

<details><summary>Test used (drop it in as <code>internal/gateway/codex_native_timeout_window_test.go</code>)</summary>

```go
package gateway

import (
	"encoding/json"
	"net/http"
	"net/http/httptest"
	"os"
	"path/filepath"
	"testing"
	"time"

	"github.com/yetone/magpie/internal/catalog"
	"github.com/yetone/magpie/internal/provider"
)

// A 500K window Codex received and cached must survive the next upstream
// model-list timeout (#1955): the fallback list is built from Codex's own
// cache, which says 500000, but the window is then restored from the
// provider's live list, which is a day old and still says the previous
// 272000 — so the answer drops back to 272000 until the upstream list is
// fetched again.
func TestCodexModelListKeepsFreshWindowOnTimeout(t *testing.T) {
	codexSignedIn(t)
	codexHome := t.TempDir()
	t.Setenv("CODEX_HOME", codexHome)
	// what Codex cached from the official 500K list
	os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(codexHome, "models_cache.json"), []byte(`{"etag":"\"v1\"","models":[
		{"slug":"gpt-6.1-sol","priority":1,"context_window":500000,"max_context_window":500000,"base_instructions":"sol prompt"}]}`), 0o644)
	// the provider's own list, last fetched a day ago, still says 272K
	if err := catalog.SaveLive("codex", provider.CodexBase, []catalog.Model{
		{ID: "gpt-6.1-sol", Context: 272000},
	}); err != nil {
		t.Fatal(err)
	}

	// the upstream model list never answers within codexModelsWait
	release := make(chan struct{})
	up := httptest.NewServer(http.HandlerFunc(func(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
		select {
		case <-release:
		case <-r.Context().Done():
		}
	}))
	defer func() { close(release); up.Close() }()
	wasBase := provider.CodexBase
	provider.CodexBase = up.URL + "/backend-api/codex"
	defer func() { provider.CodexBase = wasBase }()
	wasWait := codexModelsWait
	codexModelsWait = 200 * time.Millisecond
	defer func() { codexModelsWait = wasWait }()

	rec := httptest.NewRecorder()
	req := httptest.NewRequest("GET", CodexPath+"/models?client_version=0.162.0", nil)
	req.Header.Set("Authorization", "Bearer chatgpt-token")
	New().Handler().ServeHTTP(rec, req)

	var got struct {
		Models []struct {
			Slug    string `json:"slug"`
			Context int    `json:"context_window"`
		} `json:"models"`
	}
	json.Unmarshal(rec.Body.Bytes(), &got)
	seen := false
	for _, m := range got.Models {
		if m.Slug == "gpt-6.1-sol" {
			seen = true
			if m.Context != 500000 {
				t.Errorf("gpt-6.1-sol context_window %d after the timeout, want the cached 500000", m.Context)
			}
		}
	}
	if !seen {
		t.Fatalf("gpt-6.1-sol not in the fallback list: %s", rec.Body.String())
	}
}
```

</details>

Not tried here: a real macOS/Linux runtime, a real signed-in ChatGPT account, and post-install compaction — this is the gateway path only.

